            <ArticleTitle>Exercise induced ST segment depression preceding ST segment elevation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of exercise induced ST segment depression preceding ST segment elevation in precordial leads and persistent ST segment depression in inferior leads is reported. Such an exercise response should suggest significant fixed coronary stenosis in addition to coronary spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
